---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import QueryDiff from '../../components/QueryDiff.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="SQL Query Diff Checker" description="Compare two SQL queries line-by-line to see exactly what changed between versions.">
  <QueryDiff client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why diffing queries beats eyeballing them</h2>
  <p>Two versions of a complex query can look nearly identical at a glance while differing in one crucial WHERE condition or JOIN — a line-by-line diff makes even small but significant changes immediately visible.</p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste the original query on one side and the modified version on the other.</li>
    <li>Review the highlighted differences.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming this validates the queries.</strong> This only shows textual differences — it doesn't check whether either query is syntactically valid or produces correct results.</li>
    <li><strong>Not noticing whitespace-only differences</strong> that show up as changed lines despite representing the same logical query.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reviewing what changed in a query during a pull request</li>
    <li>Comparing a query before and after a performance optimization</li>
    <li>Auditing a query modification for unintended side effects</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this understand SQL semantics, or just text?</strong> It's a textual line-by-line diff — it doesn't understand that two differently formatted queries might be semantically equivalent.</p>
</ToolLayout>
